## Close 0.7 registry SQL deploy gap (schedules generic tasks)

Context: The 0.7 registry schema delta — widening `schedules` /
`schedule_runs` to the generic `(task_type, domain, target_key)` shape —
lived only in `schema.sql` and the app's `_ensure_schedule_task_columns`
self-heal. `make deploy` / `make bootstrap-lakebase` did not apply it, there
was no `upgrade_0.6_to_0.7.sql`, and preflight did not detect the pending
columns. An in-place 0.6→0.7 deploy could therefore leave the registry on
the legacy unique constraint until an admin re-ran Initialize.

Changes:

1. `scripts/bootstrap/lakebase-perms.sh`
   Step 2b now adds the schedules/schedule_runs columns, folds
   `drop_existing` into `config`, swaps the unique constraint, and widens
   `idx_schedule_runs_domain` (as schema owner on every Lakebase deploy).
2. `scripts/migrations/upgrade_0.6_to_0.7.sql`
   New auditable one-shot DBA migration mirroring the same DDL.
3. `scripts/_internal/_lakebase_preflight.py`
   Expects the new columns + `schedules_type_domain_target_key` so deploy
   preflight reports them as pending until bootstrap applies them.
4. `scripts/_internal/_deploy-preflight.sh`
   Requires `upgrade_0.6_to_0.7.sql` among Lakebase project files.
5. `tests/units/scripts/test_lakebase_preflight.py`
   Asserts the new EXPECTED_COLUMNS entries stay aligned with bootstrap.
6. `src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/store.py`
   Adds missing `domain_change_events` to `_KNOWN_TABLES` (diagnostics).
7. `documentation/DEPLOY_CHECKLIST.md`
   Documents the 0.6→0.7 upgrade path and lists the new migration script.
8. `scripts/update-deployed-app.sh`
   Comment now mentions the v0.7 schedules migration in the SQL step.

